{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180567231,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296aa730012pOognnQetfdRI","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_7ea9aaa202c34ec0a7c5f4ed","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: UI/Overlay System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n9: \n10: **Behavior**:\n11: - Shows on app load\n12: - Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n13: - CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n14: - Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n15: \n16: **State**:\n17: ```typescript\n18: interface IntroState {\n19:   isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n20:   isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: **UI State During Intro**:\n25: - Game renders in background\n26: - UI controls hidden\n27: - Audio may play (attract mode)\n28: \n29: ### Main Controls (HUD)\n30: \n31: **Glass HUD Container**:\n32: - Semi-transparent glass effect\n33: - Floating overlay on bottom of screen\n34: - Groups: Main controls, interaction modes, status\n35: \n36: **Main Control Buttons**:\n37: - **PLAY/PAUSE**: Toggle simulation running state\n38: - **STEP**: Execute single generation (disabled while running)\n39: - **RANDOM**: Fill grid randomly (15% cell density)\n40: - **CLEAR**: Remove all cells, reset generation (red text color)\n41: \n42: **Interaction Mode Buttons**:\n43: - **DRAW**: Enable cell placement mode (active state highlighted)\n44: - **ERASE**: Enable cell removal mode (active state highlighted)\n45: \n46: **Status Controls**:\n47: - **Waveform Selector**: Dropdown (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw)\n48: - **Volume Slider**: Range 0-0.5, 0.01 step\n49: - **Generation Counter**: Display \"GEN: {number}\"\n50: - **Settings Toggle**: Gear icon button (⚙️)\n51: \n52: ### Phase Status Display\n53: \n54: **Visibility**: Always visible\n55: \n56: **Layout**:\n57: - Shows current phase: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n58: - Timer display (visible during COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases)\n59: - Flux counter (visible during PLANNING and RUNNING phases)\n60: \n61: ### Settings Panel\n62: \n63: **Access**: Click gear icon in HUD\n64: \n65: **Configuration Options**:\n66: \n67: 1. **Speed**: Slider (10ms to 500ms)\n68: \n69: 2. **Grid Size**: Buttons for Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n70: \n71: 3. **Visuals**:\n72:    - Checkbox: Show grid lines\n73: \n74: 4. **Audio**:\n75:    - Checkbox: Enable sonification\n76: \n77: 5. **Expert Settings**:\n78:    - Access to Expert Settings panel (for tuning game parameters)\n79: \n80: **Close**: × button in header\n81: \n82: ### UI Toggle\n83: \n84: **Toggle Button**:\n85: - Icon frame (minimal)\n86: - Click to show/hide all UI\n87: - Hidden when `enableUI` prop is false (intro mode)\n88: - Position: Fixed corner\n89: \n90: ## Implementation Architecture\n91: \n92: ### State Management\n93: \n94: ```typescript\n95: interface UIState {\n96:   isUiVisible: boolean;        // Master visibility toggle\n97:   isIntro: boolean;            // Intro overlay active\n98:   isExiting: boolean;          // Intro exit animation\n99:   showSettings: boolean;       // Settings panel open\n100:   enableUI: boolean;           // Prop from App (false during intro)\n101: }\n102: ```\n103: \n104: ### Component Hierarchy\n105: \n106: ```\n107: App\n108: ├── IntroOverlay (conditional on isIntro)\n109: ├── GameOfLife\n110: │   ├── CanvasGrid\n111: │   ├── UIToggleButton\n112: │   └── GlassHUDContainer (conditional on enableUI && isUiVisible)\n113: │       ├── GlassHUD\n114: │       └── SettingsPanel (conditional on showSettings)\n115: ```\n116: \n117: ## CSS Architecture\n118: \n119: ### Glass Effect\n120: ```css\n121: .glass-hud {\n122:   background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n123:   backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n124:   border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n125:   border-radius: 12px;\n126: }\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ### Button States\n130: - **Active**: Highlighted background/border\n131: - **Disabled**: Opacity reduced, no pointer events\n132: - **Hover**: Slight brightness increase\n133: \n134: ### Animations\n135: - **Intro Exit**: Scale and fade out over 1.2s\n136: - **Panel Open**: Slide in from side\n137: - **Button Hover**: Scale/brightness transition\n138: \n139: ## Responsive Design\n140: \n141: - **Desktop**: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n142: - **Mobile**: Controls may stack or scroll\n143: - **Touch**: Minimum 44px touch targets\n144: - **Canvas**: Adapts to window size, grid scales accordingly\n145: \n146: ## Edge Cases\n147: \n148: 1. **Intro Exit**: Wait 1.2s for animation before removing component\n149: 2. **UI Hidden**: All controls invisible, toggle button still accessible\n150: 3. **Settings During Run**: Settings apply immediately, no pause required\n151: 4. **Grid Size Change**: Resets simulation\n152: 5. **Clear Grid**: Removes all cells, resets generation\n153: \n154: ## Dependencies\n155: \n156: - All systems: Configurable via settings panel\n157: - Core simulation: Speed and size settings affect simulation\n158: - Audio system: Enable toggle controls sonification\n159: - Canvas rendering: Grid line option\n160: - User interaction: Mode buttons select draw/erase\n161: - Phase management: Phase display shows current game state\n162: \n\n(End of file - total 162 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/ui-overlay.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: UI/Overlay System\n\n## Overview\nThe UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n\n**Behavior**:\n- Shows on app load\n- Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n- Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n\n**State**:\n```typescript\ninterface IntroState {\n  isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n  isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771180567158,"end":1771180567229}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180567234,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296aa79001u2i0gU7pC4t8zS","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_87945c3bfbec4de88419c177","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/scoring-system.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/scoring-system.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Scoring System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Real-time score calculation based on cellular pattern classifications, with points awarded per generation.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Scoring Formula\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ScoringConfig {\n11:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n12:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n13:   staticPointsPerGeneration: number;     // Always 0\n14:   scoreMultiplier: number;                 // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n15: }\n16: \n17: interface ScoreState {\n18:   currentScore: number;\n19:   generationScore: number;      // Score earned this generation\n20:   totalPatternsTracked: number; // Stats: total patterns ever detected\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ### Per-Generation Calculation\n25: For each generation during RUNNING phase:\n26: \n27: ```typescript\n28: function calculateGenerationScore(\n29:   trackedClusters: TrackedCluster[],\n30:   config: ScoringConfig\n31: ): number {\n32:   let generationScore = 0;\n33:   \n34:   for (const cluster of trackedClusters) {\n35:     switch (cluster.classification) {\n36:       case 'MOVER':\n37:         generationScore += config.moverPointsPerGeneration;\n38:         break;\n39:       case 'OSCILLATOR':\n40:         generationScore += config.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration;\n41:         break;\n42:       case 'STATIC':\n43:         // No points for static patterns\n44:         break;\n45:     }\n46:   }\n47:   \n48:   return generationScore * config.scoreMultiplier;\n49: }\n50: \n51: // Update score each generation\n52: scoreState.currentScore += calculateGenerationScore(clusters, config);\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Scoring Visibility\n56: - Real-time: Score updates every generation during RUNNING phase\n57: - Smooth animation: Number counting up effect (lerp over 0.2s)\n58: - Milestones: Brief flash every 100 points (optional)\n59: \n60: ## UI/UX Requirements\n61: \n62: ### Score Display\n63: - **Location**: Top-left of screen\n64: - **Format**: Large number with \"PTS\" label\n65: - **Animation**: \n66:   - Smooth increment when score changes\n67:   - Brief pulse/flash on point gain\n68:   - Color: White/bright, stands out from grid\n69: \n70: ### Pattern Breakdown (Optional)\n71: - Small sub-display showing:\n72:   - Active Movers: [count]\n73:   - Active Oscillators: [count]\n74:   - Current Rate: [points/gen]\n75: \n76: ### End-of-Level Stats\n77: Display on FINISHED phase:\n78: - Final Score: [number]\n79: - Time Survived: [seconds]\n80: - Patterns Created: [count]\n81: \n82: ## Edge Cases\n83: \n84: 1. **Score Overflow**: Cap score at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (9,007,199,254,740,991) to prevent overflow issues\n85: 2. **Negative Multiplier**: Expert settings validation should prevent negative multipliers\n86: 3. **Zero Points Generation**: Possible if no patterns active - ensure UI handles gracefully\n87: 4. **Score Calculation Lag**: If tracking takes >16ms, could delay score update - decouple from render\n88: \n89: ## Score Persistence\n90: \n91: **Per-Level Reset**: Score resets to 0 at the start of each level (no carry-over)\n92: **High Score Tracking**: Save highest score achieved per level to localStorage for player progress tracking\n93: \n94: ## Implementation Notes\n95: \n96: - Scoring must be deterministic (same patterns = same score)\n97: - Calculate in separate thread or use requestIdleCallback if heavy\n98: - Store config in expert settings with defaults:\n99:   - moverPointsPerGeneration: 10 (high reward for movement)\n100:   - oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2 (small reward for activity)\n101:   - staticPointsPerGeneration: 0 (no reward)\n102:   - scoreMultiplier: 1.0\n103: \n\n(End of file - total 103 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/scoring-system.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Scoring System\n\n## Overview\nReal-time score calculation based on cellular pattern classifications, with points awarded per generation.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Scoring Formula\n```typescript\ninterface ScoringConfig {\n  moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n  oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n  staticPointsPerGeneration: number;     // Always 0\n  scoreMultiplier: number;                 // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n}\n\ninterface ScoreState {\n  currentScore: number;\n  generationScore: number;      // Score earned this generation\n  totalPatternsTracked: number; // Stats: total patterns ever detected","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771180567163,"end":1771180567232}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180567237,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296aa7e001vdfddJYHnaOntn","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_d14d5e7c13f14623b564c167","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Phase Management\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: State machine governing the three core game phases: PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Phase Definitions\n9: \n10: #### PLANNING Phase\n11: - **Entry Condition**: Level initialization or restart\n12: - **Duration**: Unlimited (player controls when to start)\n13: - **Allowed Actions**: Place/remove cells using Flux\n14: - **START Button**: Visible and enabled when ≥1 cell placed\n15: - **Exit Condition**: Player clicks START button\n16: \n17: #### RUNNING Phase\n18: - **Entry Condition**: Countdown finishes (3, 2, 1...) after player clicked START\n19: - **Duration**: Fixed countdown timer (level-specific, starts at 45s base)\n20: - **Allowed Actions**: Cell placement using saved Flux (add-only)\n21: - **Simulation**: Game of Life rules execute automatically\n22: - **Exit Conditions**:\n23:    - Timer reaches 0 → FINISHED (score finalization)\n24:    - All cells die → FINISHED (score stops accumulating, level ends)\n25: \n26: #### FINISHED Phase\n27: - **Entry Condition**: Timer expires or all cells die\n28: - **Duration**: Brief pause before auto-advance (2.0s)\n29: - **Allowed Actions**: None (view-only)\n30: - **Outcome Display**: Show score, cells alive\n31: - **Exit Condition**: Auto-advance after 2.0s (fade transition to next level)\n32: - **Simulation**: Stops completely, no carryover to next level\n33: \n34: ### State Machine\n35: ```typescript\n36: type GamePhase = 'PLANNING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED';\n37: \n38: interface PhaseState {\n39:   current: GamePhase;\n40:   canTransition: boolean;\n41:   blockers: string[]; // Reasons why transition blocked\n42: }\n43: \n44: const transitions = {\n45:   'PLANNING': ['COUNTDOWN', 'RUNNING'],\n46:   'COUNTDOWN': ['RUNNING'],\n47:   'RUNNING': ['FINISHED'],\n48:   'FINISHED': ['PLANNING'] // Auto-triggered, circular to next level\n49: };\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ## UI/UX Requirements\n53: \n54: ### Phase Indicators\n55: - **PLANNING**:\n56:    - \"Place your cells\" text or icon\n57:    - START button prominent (enabled when ≥1 cell placed)\n58:    - Flux counter visible\n59: - **COUNTDOWN**:\n60:    - Large \"3... 2... 1...\" display\n61:    - No input accepted\n62:    - Simulation NOT running yet\n63: - **RUNNING**:\n64:    - Timer prominently displayed (countdown)\n65:    - \"Simulation Running\" indicator\n66:    - Score ticking up in real-time\n67:    - Flux counter visible (if any saved)\n68: - **FINISHED**:\n69:    - \"Time's Up\" or \"Level Complete\" message\n70:    - Final score display\n71:    - Brief stats (cells alive)\n72:    - Auto-advance countdown indicator\n73: \n74: ### Phase Transitions\n75: - **PLANNING → COUNTDOWN**:\n76:    - Player clicks START button\n77:    - Immediate transition to countdown\n78: - **COUNTDOWN → RUNNING**:\n79:    - \"3, 2, 1\" countdown completes\n80:    - Simulation starts immediately\n81:    - Sound effect: \"Simulation starting\"\n82: - **RUNNING → FINISHED**:\n83:    - Timer hits 0 OR all cells die\n84:    - Simulation stops immediately\n85:    - Sound effect: \"Level complete\" or timer expiration\n86: - **FINISHED → PLANNING** (next level):\n87:    - Fade out current screen (2.0s)\n88:    - Fade in new level (2.0s)\n89:    - Fresh grid, fresh Flux, no carryover\n90: \n91: ## Edge Cases\n92: \n93: 1. **Zero Cells at Start**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n94: 2. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops, advances to next level\n95: 3. **Browser Tab Switch**: Timer continues running when tab inactive\n96: 4. **Rapid Phase Switching**: Prevent clicking START multiple times rapidly\n97: 5. **Countdown Interrupted**: No input allowed during countdown phase\n98: 6. **Level Transition**: No simulation carryover between levels - fresh start each level\n99: \n100: ## Implementation Notes\n101: \n102: - Use React useReducer for phase state management\n103: - Add COUNTDOWN phase between PLANNING and RUNNING\n104: - Phase transitions should be guarded (can't skip phases)\n105: - Timer must use accurate timing (Date.now() or performance.now())\n106: - Simulation must NOT start until countdown completes\n107: - Level transition stops simulation completely - no carryover\n108: - Consider using a state machine library like XState if complexity grows\n109: - Log phase transitions for debugging\n110: \n\n(End of file - total 110 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/phase-management.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Phase Management\n\n## Overview\nState machine governing the three core game phases: PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Phase Definitions\n\n#### PLANNING Phase\n- **Entry Condition**: Level initialization or restart\n- **Duration**: Unlimited (player controls when to start)\n- **Allowed Actions**: Place/remove cells using Flux\n- **START Button**: Visible and enabled when ≥1 cell placed\n- **Exit Condition**: Player clicks START button\n\n#### RUNNING Phase\n- **Entry Condition**: Countdown finishes (3, 2, 1...) after player clicked START\n- **Duration**: Fixed countdown timer (level-specific, starts at 45s base)\n- **Allowed Actions**: Cell placement using saved Flux (add-only)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771180567168,"end":1771180567235}}}}
