{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180594019,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296b320001z73x5duOEikjhi","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_f1e005baecb64a9c966168c8","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check for GlassHUD component","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Search the codebase to see if there's a GlassHUD component implemented. Look for:\n- src/components/GlassHUD.tsx or similar\n- Any references to \"glass\" or \"GlassHUD\" in the codebase\n- Main UI controls implementation\n\nUse a \"quick\" thoroughness level.\n\nReturn whether GlassHUD exists and where it's located, or if it needs to be created.","command":"find GlassHUD component"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d694cd9ffeKQDTsT6evsdaF9 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Search Results\n\n### GlassHUD Component Status: ✅ EXISTS\n\nThe GlassHUD component is fully implemented but **not currently integrated** into the main Game UI.\n\n### Location\n\n**GlassHUD Component:**\n- **File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`\n- **Test File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.test.tsx`\n- **Stylesheet:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/GlassHUD.css`\n\n### GlassHUD Features Implemented\n\nThe GlassHUD component provides a glass-morphism styled UI with:\n\n**Control Buttons:**\n- START/RUNNING toggle\n- RANDOM (randomize grid)\n- CLEAR (clear grid)\n- DRAW/ERASE interaction modes\n- Grid preset selection (Small, Medium, Large)\n- Show/Hide grid toggle\n- Settings button (⚙️)\n\n**Status Display:**\n- Phase indicator\n- Live cell count\n- Flux value (with color-coded status: green/orange/red)\n\n### Current State\n\n**The Game.tsx component is NOT using GlassHUD.** Instead, it has its own inline UI controls implementation (lines 162-260 in Game.tsx). The GlassHUD component exists as a standalone component with tests, but needs to be integrated into the main game.\n\n### Related Files Found\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx` - UI visibility toggle that uses GlassHUD styles\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - References GlassHUD in implementation plan\n\n### Summary\n\nGlassHUD component **exists** and is fully implemented with styles and tests. However, it needs to be integrated into the main Game component to replace the current inline UI controls. The component is ready to use, just not currently imported or utilized in the game flow.\n</task_result>","title":"Check for GlassHUD component","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d694cd9ffeKQDTsT6evsdaF9","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771180569379,"end":1771180594018}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180607221,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296b328001UPD3hVZpuvCAJ2","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_507ff721b5664f8cace83bfb","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check UI controls implementation","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Search for main UI controls implementation in the codebase. Look for:\n- Main control buttons (PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR)\n- Interaction mode buttons (DRAW, ERASE)\n- Waveform selector, volume slider\n- Generation counter\n- Settings gear icon button\n\nUse a \"quick\" thoroughness level.\n\nReturn what controls are implemented and where they're located.","command":"find UI controls"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d694cc9ffefpMccpj4xFa29w (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my search of the codebase, here are the UI controls that are implemented and their locations:\n\n## Implemented Controls\n\n### 1. Main Control Buttons (PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR)\n**Locations:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (lines 189-203)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 57-73)\n\n**Details:**\n- **STEP button**: Advances simulation by one generation (only available in PLANNING phase)\n- **START/RUNNING button**: Starts/stops the simulation (toggles between states)\n- **CLEAR button**: Resets the grid, generation counter, and score\n- **RANDOM button**: Generates a random grid pattern with ~15% cell density\n\n### 2. Interaction Mode Buttons (DRAW, ERASE)\n**Locations:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (lines 220-234)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 77-91)\n\n**Details:**\n- **DRAW button**: Sets interaction mode to add cells (highlighted when active)\n- **ERASE button**: Sets interaction mode to remove cells (highlighted when active)\n- Both buttons are disabled during simulation runs\n\n### 3. Generation Counter\n**Location:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (line 251)\n\n**Details:**\n- Displays current generation number as `GEN: {generation}`\n- Resets to 0 when grid is cleared or randomized\n\n### 4. Settings Gear Icon Button\n**Location:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 121-123)\n\n**Details:**\n- Uses ⚙️ emoji as the icon\n- Calls `onToggleSettings` handler when clicked\n\n### Additional Controls Found\n- **Grid Size Presets**: Small, Medium, Large buttons (lines 166-184 in Game.tsx)\n- **Show/Hide Grid Toggle**: Toggles grid lines visibility (lines 209-215 in Game.tsx)\n- **UI Toggle Button**: Separate component at `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx` for hiding/showing the entire UI\n\n## NOT Implemented (Only Defined in Types)\n\n### Waveform Selector and Volume Slider\n- **Location**: Type definitions only in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts` (lines 97-101)\n- **Details**: `AudioParams` interface defines `volume: number` and `waveform: 'sine' | 'triangle' | 'square' | 'sawtooth'` but no UI controls exist to manipulate these values\n\n## Summary\nThe codebase has two main UI implementations:\n1. **Game.tsx**: A simpler, straightforward control panel with inline styles\n2. **GlassHUD.tsx**: A more polished, glass-morphism styled component with CSS classes\n\nBoth implement the same core controls, but GlassHUD.tsx appears to be a newer/better designed version with proper CSS styling classes.\n</task_result>","title":"Check UI controls implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d694cc9ffefpMccpj4xFa29w","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771180569393,"end":1771180607219}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180609013,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296b33c001whnoOHKyWhgsQs","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_21f4a64e48bc44239c81d64a","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check phase status display","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Search for phase status display implementation. Look for:\n- Phase indicator showing current phase\n- Timer display\n- Countdown display\n- Flux counter display with color coding\n\nUse a \"quick\" thoroughness level.\n\nReturn what phase status elements are implemented and where they're located.","command":"find phase status display"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d694cb4ffe0Pa2shbMXcyXL0 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my search of the codebase, here are the phase status display elements that are implemented:\n\n## Phase Status Display Implementation\n\n### 1. **Phase Indicator (Current Phase Display)**\n**Locations:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (line 248)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 128-130)\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Simple text display showing current phase: `Phase: {phaseState.current}`\n- Displays one of: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n- Located in a glass-effect status bar\n\n### 2. **Countdown Display**\n**Location:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (line 249)\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Only visible during COUNTDOWN phase\n- Format: `Countdown: {phaseState.countdownValue}`\n- Starts at 3 seconds and counts down to 0\n- Defined in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.ts` (COUNTDOWN_SECONDS = 3)\n\n### 3. **Timer Display**\n**Location:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (line 250)\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Only visible during RUNNING phase\n- Format: `Timer: {phaseState.timerRemaining}s`\n- Defaults to 45 seconds duration\n- Managed by `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts`\n- Handles tab visibility changes to ensure accurate timing\n\n### 4. **Flux Counter with Color Coding**\n**Locations:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (lines 253-259)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 42-48, 136-138)\n\n**Implementation in Game.tsx:**\n```typescript\n<div style={{\n  color: flux.current > 10 ? '#00ff00' : flux.current > 5 ? '#ffaa00' : '#ff0000',\n}}>\n  Flux: {flux.current}\n</div>\n```\n**Color coding thresholds:**\n- **Green** (#00ff00): Flux > 10\n- **Yellow/Orange** (#ffaa00): Flux 6-10\n- **Red** (#ff0000): Flux ≤ 5\n\n**Implementation in GlassHUD.tsx:**\n- Uses ratio-based color coding: `fluxColor = getFluxColor(flux, fluxMax)`\n- Red (0%), Orange (0-50%), Green (>50%)\n\n## Supporting Files\n\n**Phase State Management:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.ts` - Defines PhaseState interface and reducer\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts` - Timer/countdown logic with tab visibility handling\n\n**Related UI Components:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` - Score display (separate from phase status but often shown alongside)\n\n**Specifications:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md` - UI/UX requirements document\n\n## Summary\n\nAll four requested phase status elements are implemented:\n1. ✓ Phase indicator - Showing current phase name\n2. ✓ Timer display - During RUNNING phase only\n3. ✓ Countdown display - During COUNTDOWN phase only (3, 2, 1...)\n4. ✓ Flux counter with color coding - Three-level color system based on flux value\n\nThe displays are primarily in `Game.tsx` with additional implementations in `GlassHUD.tsx` for a more polished UI experience.\n</task_result>","title":"Check phase status display","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d694cb4ffe0Pa2shbMXcyXL0","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771180569416,"end":1771180609012}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771180632861,"sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","part":{"id":"prt_c6296aa83001NX2zdIVWG6kAg5","sessionID":"ses_39d69a733ffeSFR27erfn8OGrt","messageID":"msg_c62966bda001SJmYvaXEAUF1Dn","type":"tool","callID":"call_b6636ae0b0164cfe88375604","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore src/* codebase structure","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Explore the src/* directory structure to understand the current state of the implementation. I need to understand:\n\n1. What components exist in src/components/\n2. What libraries exist in src/lib/\n3. What types exist in src/types/\n4. What hooks exist in src/hooks/\n5. What styles exist in src/styles/\n\nFocus on understanding what has already been implemented and what might be missing. Use a \"medium\" thoroughness level.\n\nReturn a comprehensive overview of the current codebase structure, listing all files and their purposes.","command":"explore src/"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d695574ffegzqJ9OIgORFAvO (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow let me provide a comprehensive overview of the current codebase structure:\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Overview\n\nBased on my exploration of the `src/` directory, here's a complete breakdown of what has been implemented:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Components (`src/components/`)\n\n**Core Components:**\n\n- **Game.tsx** (277 lines)\n  - Main game orchestration component\n  - Manages game state (grid, flux, generation, score, phase)\n  - Handles simulation loop with 200ms interval\n  - Integrates scoring, movement detection, and phase timer\n  - Provides UI controls for grid size, interaction modes, clear/random\n\n- **CanvasGrid.tsx** (127 lines)\n  - Canvas-based grid rendering with device pixel ratio support\n  - Cell visualization with color/blur based on age\n  - Optional grid lines\n  - Responsive cell sizing (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n  - Exports CSS custom property `--life-intensity` based on active cell count\n\n- **GridInteraction.tsx** (177 lines)\n  - Handles user interactions (draw/erase cells)\n  - Manages hover state and visual feedback\n  - Integrates with flux system for cell placement limits\n  - Provides dynamic cursor feedback (crosshair/not-allowed)\n\n**UI Components:**\n\n- **ScoreDisplay.tsx** (122 lines)\n  - Displays current score with animated number transitions\n  - Pulse effect on score changes\n  - Milestone flash effect (every 100 points)\n  - Optional pattern breakdown (movers, oscillators, rate)\n  - Fixed position top-left\n\n- **GlassHUD.tsx** (145 lines)\n  - Glass-morphism HUD with controls and status display\n  - Phase status display\n  - Cell count and flux indicators with color coding\n  - Button groups for: Start/Random/Clear, Draw/Erase, Grid size, Grid toggle, Settings\n  - Responsive design\n\n- **IntroOverlay.tsx** (32 lines)\n  - Intro screen with glitch animation effect\n  - \"ENTER VOID\" button\n  - Fade-out animation on exit\n\n- **UIToggleButton.tsx** (44 lines)\n  - SVG icon button for toggling UI visibility\n  - Fixed position top-right\n  - Eye/crossed-eye icons\n\n---\n\n### 2. Libraries (`src/lib/`)\n\n**Core Simulation:**\n\n- **simulation.ts** (138 lines)\n  - Game of Life simulation logic with Conway rules\n  - Grid creation, neighbor counting, rule application\n  - Cell aging (tracks how long cells have been alive)\n  - Grid size presets (Small: 20x30, Medium: 40x50, Large: 60x80)\n  - Helper functions: countAliveCells, randomFill, clearGrid\n\n**Pattern Analysis:**\n\n- **movement.ts** (254 lines)\n  - Connected component detection (BFS algorithm)\n  - Cluster tracking across generations\n  - Centroid calculation and velocity detection\n  - Classification: MOVER, OSCILLATOR, STATIC\n  - Cluster filtering by size and counting by classification\n  - Configurable movement detection parameters\n\n**Game Systems:**\n\n- **scoring.ts** (93 lines)\n  - Score calculation based on pattern classification\n  - Points per generation: MOVER (10), OSCILLATOR (2), STATIC (0)\n  - Score formatting (K, M notation)\n  - Milestone detection (every 100 points)\n  - Configurable scoring multiplier\n\n- **flux.ts** (57 lines)\n  - Flux resource management for cell placement\n  - Cell placement and removal with refund (only during PLANNING phase)\n  - Flux color coding (green/yellow/orange/red)\n  - Tracks initial flux, placed count, removed count\n\n**Phase Management:**\n\n- **phase.ts** (166 lines)\n  - Phase state management: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED\n  - 3-second countdown\n  - 2-second finished delay\n  - Phase transition validation\n  - Blocker detection (e.g., \"Need at least 1 cell to start\")\n\n**Utilities:**\n\n- **interaction.ts** (60 lines)\n  - Grid coordinate extraction from mouse/touch events\n  - Boundary checking\n  - Interaction state management\n\n- **canvasUtils.ts** (30 lines)\n  - Cell color/blur mapping based on age (0-5 defined, 5+ defaults)\n  - Responsive cell size calculation\n  - Background and grid line colors\n\n- **state.ts** (114 lines)\n  - Reducer pattern utilities (action creators, createReducer)\n  - Async action creators\n  - combineReducers implementation\n  - localStorage helpers (save/load/remove with 'gol-' prefix)\n\n- **validation.ts** (56 lines)\n  - Coordinate validation\n  - Range checking, clamping\n  - Type guards (isPositiveNumber, isInteger, isValidRuleSet)\n  - Grid dimension validation (max 1000x1000)\n\n- **logger.ts** (46 lines)\n  - Singleton logger with debug/info/warn/error levels\n  - Timestamp formatting\n  - Development-only debug logging\n  - Error stack trace logging in dev mode\n\n---\n\n### 3. Types (`src/types/`)\n\n- **index.ts** (110 lines) - All TypeScript type definitions:\n  - `GridType` - 2D number array for grid\n  - `GamePhase` - PLANNING | COUNTDOWN | RUNNING | FINISHED\n  - `InteractionMode` - DRAW | ERASE\n  - `TransitionState` - PLAYING | FADING_OUT | INTERSTITIAL | FADING_IN | READY\n  - `CellCluster` - Cluster with id, cells (Set), centroid, generation\n  - `TrackedCluster` - Extended with centroidHistory, velocity, classification\n  - `RuleSet` - born/survive rules for simulation\n  - `SimulationState` - grid, generation, running, speed, selectedRule\n  - `FluxState` - current, initial, placed, removed\n  - `LevelConfig` - levelNumber, timeLimitSeconds, initialFlux\n  - `ScoringConfig` - points per generation, score multiplier\n  - `ScoreState` - currentScore, generationScore, totalPatternsTracked\n  - `LevelProgression` - currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, totalScore, levels\n  - `DifficultyScalingMode` - TIME_ONLY | RESOURCE_ONLY | MIXED | EXTREME\n  - `LevelGenerationParams` - baseTimeSeconds, timeIncrement, baseFlux, difficultyMode\n  - `TransitionConfig` - fade durations, interstitial duration, auto-advance, skip\n  - `MovementDetectionParams` - centroidHistoryLength, movementThreshold, minClusterSize\n  - `GridSizingParams` - mobileCellSize, desktopCellSize, minVisibleCells\n  - `AudioParams` - enabled, volume, waveform type\n  - `ExpertSettings` - Aggregates all expert parameters\n\n---\n\n### 4. Hooks (`src/hooks/`)\n\n- **usePhaseTimer.ts** (135 lines)\n  - Custom hook for managing phase timing\n  - Handles countdown and running timers\n  - Visibility change handling (tab switching)\n  - Automatic phase transitions (COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED → PLANNING)\n  - Returns: phaseState, startCountdown, startRunning, finishPhase, resetPhase\n\n---\n\n### 5. Styles (`src/styles/`)\n\n- **ScoreDisplay.css** (138 lines)\n  - Glass-morphism score display\n  - Pulse animation (scale 1.1, color flash)\n  - Milestone flash animation (scale 1.2, yellow → magenta)\n  - Responsive design (mobile adjustments)\n  - Score breakdown panel\n\n- **GlassHUD.css** (245 lines)\n  - Glass-morphism HUD with backdrop blur\n  - Button styling with hover/active states\n  - Danger button variant (red)\n  - Status indicators with color coding (green/orange/red)\n  - Slider styling for potential future controls\n  - Fully responsive (column layout on mobile)\n  - UI toggle button styling\n\n- **IntroOverlay.css** (160 lines)\n  - Glitch animation with skew effect\n  - Dual-layer pseudo-elements for RGB split effect\n  - Fade-in-scale-out exit animation\n  - Gradient sweep effect on button hover\n  - Responsive sizing\n\n- **index.css** (62 lines)\n  - Global styles and CSS variables\n  - Base typography (Inter, system-ui)\n  - Button styling\n  - Light/dark color scheme support\n  - App layout utilities\n\n---\n\n### 6. Root Level Files\n\n- **App.tsx** (8 lines)\n  - Simple wrapper that renders Game component\n\n- **main.tsx** (11 lines)\n  - Application entry point\n  - Mounts App to DOM with StrictMode\n  - Imports global styles\n\n- **test/setup.ts** (29 lines)\n  - Jest-DOM setup\n  - LocalStorage mock implementation\n  - Configures global localStorage for testing\n\n---\n\n### What's Already Implemented\n\n**Complete Systems:**\n- Core Game of Life simulation with Conway rules\n- Canvas-based grid rendering with aging visualization\n- Phase management (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n- Flux resource system for limiting cell placement\n- Pattern tracking and classification (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC)\n- Scoring system with animations and milestones\n- Responsive UI with glass-morphism design\n- Touch and mouse support for grid interaction\n- Intro overlay with glitch effects\n\n**Well-Tested:**\n- All library files have corresponding `.test.ts` files\n- All components have corresponding `.test.tsx` files\n- Test setup with localStorage mock\n\n### What Might Be Missing or Could Be Enhanced\n\n**Level System (Types defined but not implemented):**\n- Level progression system (types exist but no implementation)\n- Level generation (types defined but no logic)\n- Difficulty scaling modes (types defined but unused)\n- Time limits per level (not integrated into Game.tsx)\n\n**Audio System:**\n- AudioParams type defined but no audio implementation\n- No sound effects or background music\n\n**Transitions:**\n- TransitionState type defined but not used\n- Interstitial screens between levels (not implemented)\n\n**Expert Settings:**\n- ExpertSettings type fully defined but no UI or logic\n- Settings panel referenced in GlassHUD but not implemented\n\n**Advanced Features:**\n- Pattern library/presets\n- Save/load functionality (localStorage helpers exist but unused)\n- Undo/redo system\n- Zoom/pan controls for large grids\n\n**Performance:**\n- No optimization for very large grids\n- No web worker implementation for simulation\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe codebase represents a **well-structured, modular Game of Life implementation** with:\n- ✅ Complete core simulation and game loop\n- ✅ Beautiful glass-morphism UI with animations\n- ✅ Pattern analysis and scoring system\n- ✅ Comprehensive test coverage\n- ✅ Responsive design\n- ⚠️ Advanced features (levels, audio, settings) have types but no implementation\n- ⚠️ Some types are defined but not yet used in the application\n\nThe implementation demonstrates solid software engineering practices with clear separation of concerns, comprehensive type definitions, and good test coverage.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore src/* codebase structure","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d695574ffegzqJ9OIgORFAvO","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771180567176,"end":1771180632858}}}}
